2. Smogon usage statistics (not covered by this repository's license)
--------------------------------------------------------------------

https://www.smogon.com/stats/

data/smogon-usage/ holds Smogon's monthly usage statistics ("chaos" files),
computed by Smogon from Pokemon Showdown's ladder games: one file per supported
format, with the long tails of spreads and teammates trimmed
(data/smogon-usage/manifest.json lists each file's month, source and checksum).
They are Smogon's data, redistributed with credit so that each user needn't
download them; they are not licensed by this repository. The app never
fetches from Smogon: newer months come with a new release.


3. Fonts: Fredoka and Nunito (SIL Open Font License 1.1)
---------------------------------------------------------

suite/web/static/fonts/ holds the dashboard's two typefaces (latin and
latin-ext subsets, as Google Fonts serves them), so the suite needs no font
service. Their licence texts are next to them: OFL-Fredoka.txt (Copyright 2016
The Fredoka Project Authors) and OFL-Nunito.txt (Copyright 2014 The Nunito
Project Authors).


4. The closed-sheet set data (not covered by this repository's license)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

The packages and the models zip include tools/corpus/out/dex-tables.json
(species, moves, abilities and learnsets, generated from Pokemon Showdown's data
files - see 1.) and trainer/runs/set_prior/*.json: per species, how often each
set (item, ability, moves, nature) appears, counted from Smogon's usage
statistics (see 2.) and from public tournament team lists (Limitless). Counts
only: no
player names, teams or events.

The starter "Default" bucket (data/default_bucket.json) holds three open team
sheets from public regional results, as listed on Munchstats. The sheets carry
no player names.


5. In the Windows package only
------------------------------

The zip carries programs the setup and the app run, each under its own license,
with the license text beside it:

- Node.js (MIT, with the licenses of the components it bundles): node/LICENSE.
  https://nodejs.org
- uv (MIT or Apache-2.0, at your option): bin/uv-LICENSE-MIT and
  bin/uv-LICENSE-APACHE. https://github.com/astral-sh/uv
- Pokemon Showdown's runtime dependencies (vendor/pokemon-showdown/node_modules/,
  development tools removed): each package's license file is in its folder.

The setup downloads the rest from their own sources and installs it inside the
package's folder: Python (python-build-standalone; the PSF license), and the
Python packages in requirements/lock-win.txt plus PyTorch (from PyPI and
PyTorch's package index; each package's license is in its installed metadata,
.venv/Lib/site-packages/<package>.dist-info/).


